{"metadata":{"name":"Sunan Abu Dawud","section":{"35":{"eng-name":"Combing the Hair (Kitab Al-Tarajjul)","ara-name":"كتاب الترجل"}},"section_detail":{"35":{"hadithnumber_first":4159,"hadithnumber_last":4213,"arabicnumber_first":4159,"arabicnumber_last":4213}}},"hadiths":[{"hadithnumber":4207,"arabicnumber":4207,"text":"Ce récit ajoute (au hadith n°4194) : Mon père lui a dit (au Prophète) : « Montre-moi ce que tu as dans le dos, car je suis médecin. » Le Prophète ﷺ a répondu : « Tu n’es qu’un apaisant. Celui qui en est le médecin, c’est Celui qui l’a créé. »","grades":[{"name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih"}],"reference":{"book":35,"hadith":49},"chapter":{"id":18,"ara-name":"باب فِي الْخِضَابِ","eng-name":"Dyeing Hair","isFirstHadith":false}}]}